<TABLE WIDTH="500" BORDER="0" CELLPADDING="0" CELLSPACING="0">
	<TR><TD COLSPAN="4" WIDTH="500"><IMG SRC="/img/pix.gif" WIDTH="1" HEIGHT="10"></TD></TR>
	<TR>
		<TD>
			<CENTER><FONT FACE="Arial, Helvetica"><FONT SIZE="+2" COLOR="#003366"><B><I>The High Planes Ambassadors<BR>Code of Ethics</I></B></FONT><BR><BR>
			<B>This Code of Ethics will be followed by all High Planes Ambassadors members. Any alleged violations of this code will be heard and arbitrated before the High Council. The High Council's verdict will be <U>final</U>.</B></CENTER><BR><BR>

			<FONT SIZE="-1">
			We shall strive to assist other guild members with valor, however possible. Our brothers' and sisters' safety and well-being take priority over all other things.<BR><BR>

			We are honest and courteous in our dealings with all other players.<BR><BR>

			We will never let another citizen of Norrath die unnecessarily.<BR><BR>

			We shall not attack creatures under attack by others unless asked for help, others are clearly in trouble, or if our group's safety is at stake. We never kill-steal from another adventurer or party.  Kill-stealing is grounds for dismissal.<BR><BR>

			We never loot a corpse while battling, except in cases where the combat has been going on so long that the corpse may become open to all, or open to decay.  If we pick up a named or rare drop in such cases, we always notify our group that we are doing so/have done so, and promptly offer the loot as previously agreed by the group.<BR><BR>

			We never leave a group when corpse recovery is required until corpse recovery has been successfully completed. Leaving a group prior to successful corpse recovery without the group's full support and permission is grounds for dismissal. In case of an RL emergency or obligation, every effort will be put forward prior to camping to assure a successful corpse recovery.  We inform our groups when we start or join if any RL obligations may restrict participation; after the fact notification is unacceptable.<BR><BR>

			Intentional training of mobs onto other players is grounds for dismissal.<BR><BR>

			No cheating of any sort will be tolerated.<BR><BR>

			Requiring payment for any service performed at no actual monetary cost to the member is only allowed if the service has interrupted our ability to advance to your goal (i.e. finishing a quest, gaining a level). Members are free to accept tips or donations for any spell/services performed.<BR><BR>

			We provide our trade skills and services to other guild members for only the cost of materials, and will do so promptly if not grouped or otherwise engaged.  We offer items for sale to guild members before offering them on the open market.  Members are encouraged to donate unneeded items to guild members.<BR><BR>

			All members in good standing shall pay dues as specified. Currently, there are no guild dues.<BR><BR>

			All members must have their guild tags showing at all times.  Members may use Roleplay at their own discretion; however, Anonymous is not allowed.<BR><BR>

			All members of the guild are to be treated equally, as individuals, and always with respect.  If we have a conflict with a fellow guild member, we privately seek an officer for mediation. If the situation cannot be immediately resolved, those involved will be heard by the council.  Openly speaking sincerely disparagingly of fellow guild members is grounds for dismissal.<BR><BR>

			If we have suggestions on how the guild may be improved, we bring them forward as honorable constructive ideas, and we see them through to their ultimate consideration by High Council if necessary.  The High Planes Ambassadors cares for its members - and asks in return that its members care for the High Planes Ambassadors.
			</FONT>
		</TD>
	</TR>
